 ],
 "paragraphs": [
  {
   "domId": null,
   "fp": "Double DQN",
   "hash": "230c73c6be70730cf6a45f20b53d76415103037730f4d17b69e2daa7385cbc39",
   "id": "s0-title",
   "kind": "section_title",
   "ordinal": 1,
   "section": 0
  },
  {
   "domId": null,
   "fp": "Why the highest guess runs high, and the second opinion that fix",
   "hash": "119edabb6dbb0717e7166f3c7183f2472763cef7faefe3c03937d33ef2395c9d",
   "id": "s0-p1",
   "kind": "prose",
   "ordinal": 1,
   "section": 0
  },
  {
   "domId": null,
   "fp": "A game-playing network's guesses of how well it will do keep cli",
   "hash": "95040a9d32846152c40ffdff3f0cd7ca0242db1b23fd72022230b8693a9129a6",
   "id": "s0-p2",
   "kind": "prose",
   "ordinal": 2,
   "section": 0
  },
  {
   "domId": null,
   "fp": "The agent is the learner that picks the moves, as taught in RL B",
   "hash": "89c0483fb772e75b7fb7b2aad6d40d840e3014a4efbfc1fb1bcbf7235b20015b",
   "id": "s0-p3",
   "kind": "prose",
   "ordinal": 3,
   "section": 0
  },
  {
   "domId": null,
   "fp": "In its games the state is the screen, a move is a joystick press",
   "hash": "926e798ad65f77667884c4b1757032ebb9a7004eec0edf8ea613cfab591ce532",
   "id": "s0-p4",
   "kind": "prose",
   "ordinal": 4,
   "section": 0
  },
  {
   "domId": null,
   "fp": "An episode is one run from the start until it ends, as taught in",
   "hash": "8cd9826fcca2a58b26660d68887b1f4552a5fbd90ceef39b6522e04890184c4a",
   "id": "s0-p5",
   "kind": "prose",
   "ordinal": 5,
   "section": 0
  },
  {
   "domId": "ddqn-setup-fig",
   "fp": "Figure 1. A game screen and the bars for the presses the program",
   "hash": "1e0c0e59a88964cc4211df6ae703c064f3e86ff831d66e026320dae03ebc277c",
   "id": "s0-f1",
   "kind": "figure",
   "ordinal": 1,
   "section": 0
  },
  {
   "domId": null,
   "fp": "The screen in Figure 1 is a Breakout game, rows of blocks above ",
   "hash": "16923065b9d95badde2ead963d9e500cc482956841edef52f93f4a88de9b9869",
   "id": "s0-p6",
   "kind": "prose",
   "ordinal": 6,
   "section": 0
  },
  {
   "domId": "ddqn-problem",
   "fp": "1 Game-playing networks guess too high",
   "hash": "66e97f818f99b51f3bb4efd97144711ab265fb99751de48c33b553a685076fe5",
   "id": "s1-title",
   "kind": "section_title",
   "ordinal": 1,
   "section": 1
  },
  {
   "domId": null,
   "fp": "The return is all the reward still to come, with later rewards c",
   "hash": "780550a39e3f825102e06907e214582997e41176c6cbe90d5f159bbc1cfcc740",
   "id": "s1-p1",
   "kind": "prose",
   "ordinal": 1,
   "section": 1
  },
  {
   "domId": null,
   "fp": "A move's value , also called its score, is the return the agent ",
   "hash": "d0a130c17a1b04bf011453c2dc2994e19ec156b0ad12ecd1f2d5bb2849d0d3c4",
   "id": "s1-p2",
   "kind": "prose",
   "ordinal": 2,
   "section": 1
  },
  {
   "domId": null,
   "fp": "The discount sets how much a reward one step later still counts,",
   "hash": "7dbdd958aa6d4d53dea0c7072f379f03f6db23ca7fabc9f0f05fb7e7deacc7c7",
   "id": "s1-p3",
   "kind": "prose",
   "ordinal": 3,
   "section": 1
  },
  {
   "domId": null,
   "fp": "Training a Q-network with Q-learning's target is a Deep Q-Networ",
   "hash": "e800239eff7a09e96c0ffc8fb31306b18070e30b6da93a852f67ace4b603a8f0",
   "id": "s1-p4",
   "kind": "prose",
   "ordinal": 4,
   "section": 1
  },
  {
   "domId": null,
   "fp": "On Atari those scores end above the return the learned policy re",
   "hash": "bbbb06129f9c3776fdb9e389f33e330e63475a21470ca7b78e9abc1ba7dc4862",
   "id": "s1-p5",
   "kind": "prose",
   "ordinal": 5,
   "section": 1
  },
  {
   "domId": "ddqn-high-fig",
   "fp": "Figure 2. DQN's estimate climbs above the return its policy real",
   "hash": "45f2f45414e8a36ce5e00c2073bcc96ba6ae656f2ed664da1891c28aca8139ee",
   "id": "s1-f1",
   "kind": "figure",
   "ordinal": 1,
   "section": 1
  },
  {
   "domId": null,
   "fp": "In Figure 2, the red line is DQN's estimate, the teal line Doubl",
   "hash": "f46e52cf5eaffe2fffab6f884a12b52eb9d29d63373c95eeaf395587743bc5ec",
   "id": "s1-p6",
   "kind": "prose",
   "ordinal": 6,
   "section": 1
  },
  {
   "domId": "overestimation",
   "fp": "2 Why the max runs high",
   "hash": "11e1006a2ca1f4c061a98fd8019bbee8ad7bc42c035cf2447b1d79f8651485dc",
   "id": "s2-title",
   "kind": "section_title",
   "ordinal": 1,
   "section": 2
  },
  {
   "domId": null,
   "fp": "The max picks the luckiest guess",
   "hash": "c63c812d065e4fa914bf247917336dd8b5bb928999de40b3b6259a41f78bad68",
   "id": "s2-p1",
   "kind": "prose",
   "ordinal": 1,
   "section": 2
  },
  {
   "domId": null,
   "fp": "What. Picture one screen where every press is truly worth the sa",
   "hash": "2e673bd12e7d86fdb7b94b1bc6c6f2e0fa6bbb43d31e0cece914426082fe29f5",
   "id": "s2-p2",
   "kind": "prose",
   "ordinal": 2,
   "section": 2
  },
  {
   "domId": null,
   "fp": "How. The max takes the highest guess, so it picks the press whos",
   "hash": "f436caf40cb102463aae2a60b7c386da9db03019be05f7e49fb9fb2e8559ca0e",
   "id": "s2-p3",
   "kind": "prose",
   "ordinal": 3,
   "section": 2
  },
  {
   "domId": null,
   "fp": "Why. When it works, the scores climb above the points the progra",
   "hash": "d14c9d7a3065f170a6403310045f253625bff8486705ec01df859b52839dfd17",
   "id": "s2-p4",
   "kind": "prose",
   "ordinal": 4,
   "section": 2
  },
  {
   "domId": null,
   "fp": "Bootstrapping means putting your own current guess for the next ",
   "hash": "b24698e097d4167e3d21178b9e57e4b56834440cc9c4b96fc2e8734b96bab5bd",
   "id": "s2-p5",
   "kind": "prose",
   "ordinal": 5,
   "section": 2
  },
  {
   "domId": null,
   "fp": "Overestimation means the values climb above the return the agent",
   "hash": "e7339a3e6c16aeeb5da0a3d7b698abc230447e01abd1b43e1cbbf98457aec054",
   "id": "s2-p6",
   "kind": "prose",
   "ordinal": 6,
   "section": 2
  },
  {
   "cardOrdinal": 1,
   "domId": "ddqnBiasEq",
   "fp": "Equation 1. This card shows the average of that highest guess si",
   "hash": "a3a35af75433b6098ccc1c0aef13b23e41b9fd54dfd4837cdbdc309ed59a0858",
   "id": "s2-e1",
   "kind": "equation",
   "ordinal": 1,
   "section": 2
  },
  {
   "domId": null,
   "fp": "Equation 1. This card shows the average of that highest guess si",
   "hash": "c493703a1ab05aa21a04b3af42195c62f79fd908dafa8c28358147d2f90eafef",
   "id": "s2-p7",
   "kind": "prose",
   "ordinal": 7,
   "section": 2
  },
  {
   "cardOrdinal": 1,
   "domId": null,
   "eqLine": "1",
   "fp": "Intuition. A max over noisy guesses runs high: the luckiest gues",
   "hash": "98a7356df1277aaa9b609b7843671a2f065abeccd5f8064a5aea8ddc4453a252",
   "id": "s2-e1-l1",
   "kind": "eqwhy",
   "labeled": true,
   "labels": [
    "Intuition.",
    "The mathematics.",
    "Example."
   ],
   "ordinal": 1,
   "section": 2
  },
  {
   "cardOrdinal": 1,
   "domId": null,
   "eqLine": "2",
   "fp": "Intuition. Averaging each move first lets the lucky errors cance",
   "hash": "305f29ac735c43aa517df98d5b69c77620e50387d836b736e55870e354bf4853",
   "id": "s2-e1-l2",
   "kind": "eqwhy",
   "labeled": true,
   "labels": [
    "Intuition.",
    "The mathematics.",
    "Example."
   ],
   "ordinal": 2,
   "section": 2
  },
  {
   "domId": "ddqn-max-fig",
   "fp": "Figure 3. Each dot is a guess, and the highest sits above the li",
   "hash": "36a4d6ed2e6f3e5a14fe46c269421b9f8888ebf668f8d7f99e0f28c84a7c657c",
   "id": "s2-f1",
   "kind": "figure",
   "ordinal": 1,
   "section": 2
  },
  {
   "domId": null,
   "fp": "Figure 3 shows why the max of noisy guesses runs high. Take the ",
   "hash": "9f52658b187b8e93615ffc7292dd44e171d95a691d81019ebd94bcc6538d2604",
   "id": "s2-p8",
   "kind": "prose",
   "ordinal": 8,
   "section": 2
  },
  {
   "domId": null,
   "fp": "The Double DQN paper proves that even fair guesses, right on ave",
   "hash": "72ca0e5effe7902b3bdea02ffae050c19e350f5088d96d961eef5b0b25b6e5a2",
   "id": "s2-p9",
   "kind": "prose",
   "ordinal": 9,
   "section": 2
  },
  {
   "domId": "ddqn-idea",
   "fp": "3 A second opinion from the target network",
   "hash": "4a310784a166cb1018fb28990d7491a833948c258eed7d947dfdff063f31e15b",
   "id": "s3-title",
   "kind": "section_title",
   "ordinal": 1,
   "section": 3
  },
  {
   "domId": null,
   "fp": "A second opinion on the pick",
   "hash": "072d11b0a1f5ce439bfb2c60e9f5ecf706ea9776262a7b3d0da9bfe9ddf3c864",
   "id": "s3-p1",
   "kind": "prose",
   "ordinal": 1,
   "section": 3
  },
  {
   "domId": null,
   "fp": "What. Picture two sets of guesses for the same next screen. Doub",
   "hash": "8aff155f67905b0464f180e665af68229b3d927578ef05e2c9d56cce3bb5e9c3",
   "id": "s3-p2",
   "kind": "prose",
   "ordinal": 2,
   "section": 3
  },
  {
   "domId": null,
   "fp": "How. Double DQN uses the live network, the one being trained, to",
   "hash": "b6f9378e8c5fce03a6669ef0c0fcfd61e0bf7d989be17ef2c91b5a8271e244ef",
   "id": "s3-p3",
   "kind": "prose",
   "ordinal": 3,
   "section": 3
  },
  {
   "domId": null,
   "fp": "Why. When it works, the target sits near the points the program ",
   "hash": "991fdda32a0e66d24474220abec65039b97eed0258cfc0eccbcdffb5e1518569",
   "id": "s3-p4",
   "kind": "prose",
   "ordinal": 4,
   "section": 3
  },
  {
   "domId": null,
   "fp": "In Double Q-learning the roles switch at random from update to u",
   "hash": "53f1c2723f0b7ef16f014c43fa1f71e45fe2f9c3d19c25fb740ac8ff3a54824a",
   "id": "s3-p5",
   "kind": "prose",
   "ordinal": 5,
   "section": 3
  },
  {
   "domId": "ddqn-big-fig",
   "fp": "Figure 4. The next screen goes to each network, and the score th",
   "hash": "832d9c8520dfdb5c345ca000783730fec00f743c65c096c081fa35cae2f7b007",
   "id": "s3-f1",
   "kind": "figure",
   "ordinal": 1,
   "section": 3
  },
  {
   "domId": null,
   "fp": "In Figure 4 the next screen goes to both networks: the live netw",
   "hash": "6d8cb57732668b6c40e1ed96b8a3c731db236b051828760fb7886288f651eb1c",
   "id": "s3-p6",
   "kind": "prose",
   "ordinal": 6,
   "section": 3
  },
  {
   "domId": null,
   "fp": "The target network is a copy of the live one that trails behind ",
   "hash": "41a57a7e2c53debf4dbfca70e00f113501edb2883d7e167c94bb4ef0ce722357",
   "id": "s3-p7",
   "kind": "prose",
   "ordinal": 7,
   "section": 3
  },
  {
   "domId": "ddqn-two-fig",
   "fp": "Figure 5. The top row picks the move; the bottom row scores that",
   "hash": "1ac2445ec89ffea731db28d05c383d9c6354bd960376cfb5ccd62c2413369ac5",
   "id": "s3-f2",
   "kind": "figure",
   "ordinal": 2,
   "section": 3
  },
  {
   "domId": null,
   "fp": "Take a screen in Figure 5 where the live row's highest dot sits ",
   "hash": "86c4b9ebc5afe213a9bf141eb9670e80acaa9b1e0a72783d98740a1429785376",
   "id": "s3-p8",
   "kind": "prose",
   "ordinal": 8,
   "section": 3
  },
  {
   "domId": "ddqn-target",
   "fp": "4 The target splits the pick from the score",
   "hash": "aec3fd667ea1bb82ede9641834c41cc029e814681f59189de0258653b16ae9c6",
   "id": "s4-title",
   "kind": "section_title",
   "ordinal": 1,
   "section": 4
  },
  {
   "domId": null,
   "fp": "One network picks, the other scores",
   "hash": "a29066f9a9cfd5e3a9190b848474045391e0f5409b7801a6ecd048a515ff4510",
   "id": "s4-p1",
   "kind": "prose",
   "ordinal": 1,
   "section": 4
  },
  {
   "domId": null,
   "fp": "What. Picture one step the program already played, and the scree",
   "hash": "a51eeabce382bc688d6f22eb12a46f415ae095bf77e6b70fe9ec071dbf355e5d",
   "id": "s4-p2",
   "kind": "prose",
   "ordinal": 2,
   "section": 4
  },
  {
   "domId": null,
   "fp": "How. The live network picks the next move with argmax, the move ",
   "hash": "5701c76901b3723ad5399b38a62271b31bcc8487d06e3e27d1b9fe4f67449197",
   "id": "s4-p3",
   "kind": "prose",
   "ordinal": 3,
   "section": 4
  },
  {
   "domId": null,
   "fp": "Why. When it works, the bars settle near the points the program ",
   "hash": "f5290baf24d4b1e438cbd8a694d95557839dc18573539f92424e65f539d0170b",
   "id": "s4-p4",
   "kind": "prose",
   "ordinal": 4,
   "section": 4
  },
  {
   "domId": null,
